        {
          "type": "turn_end",
          "turn": {
            "text": "Alberto's Fraud Detection Agent is built for an online event ticketing platform. It reviews newly published events and organizers, providing approve/reject/request-info recommendations with reasons for a human admin. The agent operates with graded autonomy: it auto-approves only on evidence verified in code, while web sources can hold decisions back but never approve them.\n\nDuring offline evaluations across 31 cases, the local 9B model reduced approved fraud from 54% to 8% over twelve iterations, and eliminated fraud approved without human review (from 27% to 0%). Claude Haiku 5.5 was chosen for deployment, achieving 86% accuracy versus 71%, with only 1% of fraud approved versus 8%. It costs about $0.002 per review. The stack includes TypeScript, PostgreSQL, and GCP.",
            "toolCalls": [],
            "stopReason": "end_turn",
